Do not export loader variables when running the build interpreter.

configure sets RUNSHARED so that make runs ./python with LD_LIBRARY_PATH (or,
with the EasyBuild patch this replaces, LD_PRELOAD) naming the build
directory. Every program the test suite starts inherits that. A preloaded
libpython built against a newer glibc than the host's cannot be loaded by
host programs, which then exit before main.

RUNSHARED is left empty. The build's libpython is found through the run path
instead: the EasyBuild RPATH wrappers put <installdir>/lib first in every
binary, and the easyconfig links the build's libpython there for the build
and test steps. A run path to the build directory itself cannot be used: the
wrappers filter the build directory out of -rpath=DIR arguments and place
any other spelling behind the compatibility layer's library directory.

--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -7737,7 +7737,8 @@
     Linux*|GNU*|NetBSD*|FreeBSD*|DragonFly*|OpenBSD*|VxWorks*)
       LDLIBRARY='libpython$(LDVERSION).so'
       BLDLIBRARY='-L. -lpython$(LDVERSION)'
-      RUNSHARED=LD_LIBRARY_PATH=`pwd`${LD_LIBRARY_PATH:+:${LD_LIBRARY_PATH}}
+      # Build executables resolve libpython through their run path.
+      RUNSHARED=''
 
       # The Android Gradle plugin will only package libraries whose names end
       # with ".so".

--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -1580,7 +1580,8 @@
     Linux*|GNU*|NetBSD*|FreeBSD*|DragonFly*|OpenBSD*|VxWorks*)
       LDLIBRARY='libpython$(LDVERSION).so'
       BLDLIBRARY='-L. -lpython$(LDVERSION)'
-      RUNSHARED=LD_LIBRARY_PATH=`pwd`${LD_LIBRARY_PATH:+:${LD_LIBRARY_PATH}}
+      # Build executables resolve libpython through their run path.
+      RUNSHARED=''
 
       # The Android Gradle plugin will only package libraries whose names end
